  "aciklama": "In 1944, Mount Vesuvius erupted in the middle of World War II, burying villages and destroying dozens of Allied bombers. The failure mechanism: heavy ash fall and lava flows.\n\nFailure chain: Magma recharges → Lava flows down slopes → In 1944, Mount Vesuvius erupted — and dozens of American B-25 bombers sitting at Pompeii Airfield were caught beneath falling volcanic ash.\n\nHow can a volcano destroy aircraft without lava ever touching them?\n\nThis short reconstructs what happened at Pompeii Airfield during the 1944 eruption of Mount Vesuvius.\n\nWatch next: How a Single Step Triggers an Avalanche\nhttps://youtu.be/ODZ7y6r1o6o\n\nFootage & sources:\n• “Vesuvius in Eruption, newsreel (1944)” — Wikimedia Commons\n• Mount Vesuvius — Wikipedia\n• Pompeii Airfield — Wikipedia\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Archival footage is authentic or appropriately licensed. Reconstructed scenes are labelled on screen.\n\n#MountVesuvius #WWII #B25 #EngineeringDisaster #Shorts",
